{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Thus</b> — Some say that <b>the covenant of brothers</b> concerns Solomon, who made a covenant with Hiram king of Tyre, and he called him <i>brother</i>. But this is not the peshat; it is only midrash. For they were not brothers at all, and Tyre does not <i>return</i> [in the accusation] — only Edom, who is Israel's brother truly, from father and mother. The explanation is that Tyre saw Edom sought Israel's harm more than all the nations, and did not remember the covenant of brothers; therefore it delivered Israel to Edom to take vengeance on them."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:43.379446133Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}